{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656362-builing-a-lair-thoughts-and-questions","id":656362,"title":"Builing a Lair - Thoughts and questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-08T04:43:56-07:00","id":656362,"title":"Builing a Lair - Thoughts and questions","content":"My goal in creating this thread is to discuss, collect and disseminate ideas and advice about Lairs. Everything from homebrew Traits to thoughts on how to tie together various Chambers thematically has a place here. I do expect it to cover Q&amp;A so don't be shy about it either - I have a few queries of my own. I am only going to try and keep track of Lair based stuff here though.<br /> <br /> This post will be edited frequently to keep the Master list up to date.<br /> <br /> <b>Traits:</b><ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait\">New Trait: Wonderous</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656362-builing-a-lair-thoughts-and-questions\">New Trait: Demolished</a></li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 09-09-2015, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T05:04:55-07:00","id":656388,"title":"","content":"I said I had a couple of questions; well here is some of them. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>How large is a single Chamber? Are we talking a single bedroom or a snow-capped mountain? A single storied house or 500 square metre garden maze? A subway station or the minimart at a petrol station? A forest clearing or the whole darn woods? Obviously there is some wiggle room here and multiple answers can be right but there is a limit. Some help identifying the line would be nice.</li> <li>How can non-Beast supernaturals 'stumble' on a Lair? I'm mainly thinking of how one of the Lost or the Awakened could conceivably enter the Primordial Dream (and subsequently a Bedgotten's Chamber). The simple answer of &quot;can't happen&quot; is less interesting story wise than the alternative.</li> <li>While individuals will react according their character; what do you think the general reaction for 'chamber-napping' is? By 'chamber-napping' I mean claiming a site as Chamber only to find out later that another Beast already has it in their Lair and now you're both Broodmates...It get's more complicated if the individuals in question already are a part of separate Broods. Technically, the RAW says that this just 'merges' the Broods but I doubt human psychology plus monstrous territoriality would let it be that simple. Of course you don't have to like your Brood so...<b>[Clarification:</b> Not asking for mechanical advice on this one, RAW works fine by me here.<b>]</b></li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T22:10:22-07:00","id":657403,"title":"","content":"I thought up a rough idea for a lair trait as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Demolished</b><br /> <br /> Your soul is a thing of rage and hatred that mankind can not tame. It lashes at everything around it in an effort to vent its frustration. The landscape of your lair takes on a perilous form with fissures gouged into the earth, buildings in a condemned status, trees snapped like tooth picks and other symptoms of a natural disaster having torn its way through the place. Attempting to travel through any chambers with this trait are more difficult for one's enemies, as they must navigate the unstable terrain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T23:08:01-07:00","id":657426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656362-builing-a-lair-thoughts-and-questions?p=656388#post656388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How large is a single Chamber? Are we talking a single bedroom or a snow-capped mountain? A single storied house or 500 square metre garden maze? A subway station or the minimart at a petrol station? A forest clearing or the whole darn woods? Obviously there is some wiggle room here and multiple answers can be right but there is a limit. Some help identifying the line would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would set the base at the size of wherever the chamber was initially created. Like it wouldn't be too hard to believe that a chamber made in a forest and as a forest would be a similar size or that one created in the image of the apartment it happened in would be the same size. That said I would also say they have that vague sort of nightmare quality to them that makes it so the chambers are basically as big as they need to be in spite of a reasonable size. Like a locker room fashioned chamber that has the Maze trait could somehow enable a person to wander for miles<br /> and miles without encountering an area they've been before even though no locker room occupies a space listed in miles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656362-builing-a-lair-thoughts-and-questions?p=656388#post656388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can non-Beast supernaturals 'stumble' on a Lair? I'm mainly thinking of how one of the Lost or the Awakened could conceivably enter the Primordial Dream (and subsequently a Bedgotten's Chamber). The simple answer of &quot;can't happen&quot; is less interesting story wise than the alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well I can't speak from the etherial elements, but there are a few I can think of. The most obvious would be entering when the Beast has already opened the door to the lair. Like using Skeleton Key to force open a portal to the Lair and someone else going through before the portal has closed, or if you wanted to go with an odd coincidence have it happen because the Beast altered the destination while the other was in transit. Another would be walking in when a Beast has caused their Lair to suffuse an area through their tilts.<br /> <br /> As for less standard methods. I would say if you try accessing an areas umbral counterpart without a clear idea of what it looks like then you might be able to force open the door to a chamber if you're using the room a chamber was created in or recently accessed from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656362-builing-a-lair-thoughts-and-questions?p=656388#post656388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While individuals will react according their character; what do you think the general reaction for 'chamber-napping' is? By 'chamber-napping' I mean claiming a site as Chamber only to find out later that another Beast already has it in their Lair and now you're both Broodmates...It get's more complicated if the individuals in question already are a part of separate Broods. Technically, the RAW says that this just 'merges' the Broods but I doubt human psychology plus monstrous territoriality would let it be that simple. Of course you don't have to like your Brood so...<b>[Clarification:</b> Not asking for mechanical advice on this one, RAW works fine by me here.<b>]</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The one who owned the old chamber is probably going to be annoyed. I mean it gets harder to make a chamber in an area that already has one, so you had to force it. Not helped that you've not forcefully connected your lair and their lair, plus any existing broods, so I think fighting or at least arguing will come up over who has the right to the chamber and if no compromise can be reached it may eventually just move to one of them being made to destroy the offending chamber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T23:17:26-07:00","id":657427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656362-builing-a-lair-thoughts-and-questions?p=657426#post657426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one who owned the old chamber is probably going to be annoyed. I mean it gets harder to make a chamber in an area that already has one, so you had to force it. Not helped that you've not forcefully connected your lair and their lair, plus any existing broods, so I think fighting or at least arguing will come up over who has the right to the chamber and if no compromise can be reached it may eventually just move to one of them being made to destroy the offending chamber.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that the Begotten attitude towards fate and family is worth remembering here, particularly given that Beasts can recognize Chambers from either side of the waking/dreaming divide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T09:05:46-07:00","id":657948,"title":"","content":"Context definitely plays a role in determining the size and detail of a Chamber. A Chamber based on a Skyscraper drawing inspiration from a height-induced panic attack will be less detailed than one inspired by homicidal rage carried out within one of its tenements, at least in regard to the tenement in question.<br /> <br /> A non-Beast finding their way into a Lair would be as difficult, if not more difficult than casting sympathetic magic on the Beast itself, in that at the very least the character would have to know that a Beast makes it Lair there.<br /> <br /> It depends on the Beasts in question, and local Begotten politics. If the Hive is a central political unit, and mutual support is an encouraged and accepted practice, than there shouldn't be any more enmity than normal for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 09-16-2015, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T17:33:14-07:00","id":667635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656362-builing-a-lair-thoughts-and-questions?p=656388#post656388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .How can non-Beast supernaturals 'stumble' on a Lair? I'm mainly thinking of how one of the Lost or the Awakened could conceivably enter the Primordial Dream (and subsequently a Bedgotten's Chamber). The simple answer of &quot;can't happen&quot; is less interesting story wise than the alternative. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd look long and hard at the Dreamspeaker Legacy. They talk extensively about &quot;the Dreamborn&quot; and &quot;the Dream&quot;. And they even have a new Merit, &quot;Dream Lands&quot; . . . which certainly seems like it overlaps with the turf of the Begotten . . .<br /> <br /> Now, the Legacy was developed long, <i>long </i>before <b>Beast</b> was even conceived of . . . But of all the mages, they seem the most likely to have the power to drop in on a Beast unannounced.<br /> <br /> I'd also give a hard look at the Clavicularius. Not only do they specialize in goetic magics (and the Begotten have been described as &quot;super goetics&quot;), but they're known for building sanctuaries and retreats in the Temenos, which is right next to the Primordial Dream . . . The Key Bearers would likely be fascinated with (and possibly horrified by) the existence of the Begotten, and it wouldn't surprise me to learn that they could adapt their signature rotes to the task. Or find themselves stranded there, after a particularly spectacular failure . . .<br /> <br /> But something that might be an option for anyone - supernatural or mundane - to visit a Lair would be in dreams. A Begotten is a primal fear made manifest, its Lair composed of human nightmares. It seems reasonable that people sleeping (and dreaming) in the mundane counterpart to a Chamber might find themselves accidentally stumbling through that Begotten's private realm . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T08:41:47-07:00","id":673226,"title":"","content":"One of Dave's spoilers mentioned that the Primordial Dream is a known part of astral space, right on the border of the temenos and anima mundi. Mages can stumble into beast's lairs just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T09:42:03-07:00","id":673272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656362-builing-a-lair-thoughts-and-questions?p=673226#post673226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of Dave's spoilers mentioned that the Primordial Dream is a known part of astral space, right on the border of the temenos and anima mundi. Mages can stumble into beast's lairs just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The big problem being, as noted, it's <s>dark and full of terrors</s> old and deep and covered in hostile effects and even-more-hostile fearmonsters who live there, along with being a complete side-trip from the more conventional reason mages travel that far into the Temenos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T18:29:37-07:00","id":674771,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to remember - was there a &quot;Scaling&quot; Lair trait? Something that skews sizes within the Lair? Seems kind of thematically appropriate for some of the larger Souls/Horrors - allowing them to furnish their Lairs with regular gear/furniture, while keeping intruders tiny and disadvantaged<br /> <br /> And . . . I've gotten fixated on the idea of an Anakim keeping prisoners in a giant bird cage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . . . but its not like you can just wander down to Walmart and buy a fifty foot tall one. Ooo! Or a giant hamster habitat - can't you just see the prisoners running on the exercise wheel?<br /> <br /> (I can just picture the giant tapping the cage, saying &quot;Sing for me, little birdy&quot;, while a Hero carries the Anakim's sewing needle like a sword, sneaking in through a mouse hole . . . )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 09-22-2015, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T18:40:21-07:00","id":674777,"title":"","content":"There's no Scaling trait but there is a No Exits trait, which might be what you are looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T19:28:10-07:00","id":674802,"title":"","content":"I'm still not certain if each Lair chamber is supposed to stay an exact replica of the place it's based off of or if it's supposed to slowly warp into a nightmarish otherworld version.<br /> <br /> I know which I prefer, I just don't know which one is supposed to be true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T20:04:51-07:00","id":674864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656362-builing-a-lair-thoughts-and-questions?p=674802#post674802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not certain if each Lair chamber is supposed to stay an exact replica of the place it's based off of or if it's supposed to slowly warp into a nightmarish otherworld version.<br /> <br /> I know which I prefer, I just don't know which one is supposed to be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect from the descriptions of the Lair as a whole that the exact replica interpretation is limited to the immediate scene of the Chamber's genesis at best.<br /> <br /> Something to hope the Player's Guide covers in at least moderate detail, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T01:37:36-07:00","id":675029,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"right\">Until we will pursue random speculation!</div> I'm just going to use the initial chamber location with whatever incident played up and additional elements (read <i>Traits</i>) from the Lair added.<br /> <br /> Question 4) Does imposing your Lair Traits upon a location count for fulfilling that requirement for claiming it as a Chamber? This doesn't cover either the Integrity (or equivalent.) loss or Exceptional Success on a Nightmare roll &amp; the spending of Satiety to claim it. I'm only asking if placing the Trait counts as the location having the trait for this purpose.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T11:13:31-07:00","id":675443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656362-builing-a-lair-thoughts-and-questions?p=675029#post675029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question 4) Does imposing your Lair Traits upon a location count for fulfilling that requirement for claiming it as a Chamber?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can only do that on places that aren't already one of your Chambers if one of your Traits is already present, so\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T14:30:48-07:00","id":675704,"title":"","content":"There<i> is</i> one possible scenario where this would come up: if you force it via physical similarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T15:06:17-07:00","id":675733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656362-builing-a-lair-thoughts-and-questions?p=675704#post675704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There<i> is</i> one possible scenario where this would come up: if you force it via physical similarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Broodmates' Traits are specifically called out in Chapter Seven's section on the Lair as a means of getting the appropriate resonance to add a Chamber, which suggests the way the Trait got there is largely irrelevant for that purpose.<br /> <br /> Though I must say it's a rather monomaniacal Beast to hypothetically take up multiple Chamber slots with the same basic type of location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-23-2015, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T20:31:49-07:00","id":698330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656362-builing-a-lair-thoughts-and-questions?p=656388#post656388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can non-Beast supernaturals 'stumble' on a Lair? I'm mainly thinking of how one of the Lost or the Awakened could conceivably enter the Primordial Dream (and subsequently a Bedgotten's Chamber). The simple answer of &quot;can't happen&quot; is less interesting story wise than the alternative. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Still playing with this idea in my head:<br /> <br /> One possibility (to stumble onto a Lair or into the Primordial Dream) might be abusing Skeleton Key. Its not a &quot;normal&quot; way to open a gate - this Beast ability is akin to ripping a door off the hinges. Repeatedly using Skeleton Key on a gate should probably have some consequences. <i>Things</i> from the other side slipping through, the gate randomly opening by itself . . . Or the gate opening to <i>other</i> places. As the Beast's actions progressively warp the gate . . . why not have it start opening into the Primordial Dream? <br /> <br /> Or, going back to the idea of mage Legacies . . . I could see the Tamers of Fire and the Tamers of Stone getting involved with Heroes. Both Legacies require their members to protect the Sleepers and stand against the terrors of the night<br /> <br /> And then there are the Fangs of Mara . . . An entire Legacy of mages dedicated to mastering fear, and understanding nightmare creatures. Depending on the circumstances, they could easily ally with or end up opposing the Begotten (as many Nightmares are deeply scarred by their own fears). Or, as befits a Left-Hand Legacy, they might decide to start vivisecting the Children to understand them better . . .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}